  "guid": "com.ghost.variableraidtimer",
  "name": "Variable Raid Timer",
  "slug": "variable-raid-timer",
  "teaser": "A mod to spice things up a bit, and remind you there's a timer to check",
  "thumbnail": "https://forge-static.sp-tarkov.com/mods/rmOQUuiJOG31J6VelFSfa6kQWSWtTvwclRYoJ9CW.jpg",
  "downloads": 368,
  "favourites_count": 6,
  "description": "<p>Description</p>\n<p>A server mod for SPT 4.0+ that randomizes raid duration on every raid start, forcing you to actually check the timer and adapt their strategy accordingly.</p>\n<p>Got a long raid? Pace yourself. Loot, explore, but don’t forget to check your doors and corners. That’s how they get you, kid.</p>\n<p>Got a short raid? Forget about looting and haul ass out of there.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Installation</p>\n<p>Like the other mods. You extract the contents of the 7z archive into your main SPT folder.</p>\n<p>That’s it.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Configuration</p>\n<p>Edit config.json to adjust the behaviour:</p>\n<pre><code>\"MaxVariancePercent\"\n</code></pre>\n<p>Maximum deviation from the map’s base raid time, as a percentage.<br />\nA value of <code>20</code> means the raid time can vary by up to +-20% of the base duration.</p>\n<pre><code>\"Bias\"\n</code></pre>\n<p>Controls the probability of getting a longer or shorter raid. Lower values means chance leans towards shorter raids. 0 is shorter raids only. 10 is effectively only longer raids.</p>\n<pre><code>\"MinimumRaidTimeMinutes\"\n</code></pre>\n<p>Hard floor in minutes. The randomized time will never go below this value regardless of variance.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Compatibility</p>\n<p>SPT 4.0.0+</p>\n<p>I have not tested with Fika, and I don’t intend to.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Disclaimer</p>\n<p>I’m fairly new to coding, so the code contains AI-assisted content. Also, expect bugs.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Special thanks to Sgtlaggy for his help reading the code and pointing out everything wrong with it</p>\n",
